{% extends 'base.en.html.twig' %}
{% set nav_actif = 'apropos' %}
{% set route_fr = 'paleo_apropos' %}
{% set route_de = 'paleo_de_apropos' %}

{% block titre %}About the author{% endblock %}
{% block meta_description %}Marie-Noëlle Kreilos, the author of this blog: musical palaeography in Strasbourg, music teaching in Schaffhausen, president of ERTA — the background behind Paléo.{% endblock %}

{% block contenu %}
<h1>About the author</h1>
<p class="chapeau">
    <strong>Marie-Noëlle Kreilos</strong> — musician, teacher, and the author of this
    blog. <em>Paléo</em> grew out of her own path, between the classroom and the
    study room.
</p>

<div class="encadre def">
    <span class="etiquette">Where the name “Paléo” comes from</span>
    <p>
        Between 1994 and 1996, Marie-Noëlle Kreilos studied <strong>musical
        palaeography</strong> at the <strong>University of Strasbourg</strong>&nbsp;:
        the discipline that deciphers old musical writing — the very one that gave this
        blog its name. That taste for neumes and old manuscripts never left her&nbsp;:
        <em>Paléo</em> is its continuation, meant to pass it on simply.
    </p>
</div>

<h2>Background</h2>
<div class="fiche">
    <dl>
        <dt>1987 – 1990</dt><dd>Recorder teaching diploma <span class="mot-latin">(Lehrdiplom Blockflöte)</span>, Bundesakademie Trossingen</dd>
        <dt>1990 – 1994</dt><dd>Postgraduate diploma in musicology <span class="mot-latin">(Musikwissenschaft und Schulmusik)</span>, University of Strasbourg</dd>
        <dt>1994 – 1996</dt><dd>Musical palaeography, University of Strasbourg</dd>
        <dt>1990 – 2012</dt><dd>Music teacher at the Musikschule of Schaffhausen, Switzerland</dd>
        <dt>Since 2013</dt><dd>DELF/DALF examiner (official French-as-a-foreign-language exams)</dd>
        <dt>Since 2015</dt><dd>President of ERTA <span class="mot-latin">(European Recorder Teachers Association)</span></dd>
    </dl>
</div>

<p class="lettrine">
    One foot in music teaching, the other in the study of old manuscripts&nbsp;: this
    dual background gives <em>Paléo</em> its particular tone — that of a teacher used
    to making technical knowledge accessible, applied here to a thousand-year-old
    script.
</p>

<div class="encadre astuce">
    <span class="etiquette">Interests</span>
    <p>
        Fighting poverty, education, arts and culture, human rights, animal welfare,
        the environment.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="encadre">
    <span class="etiquette">A word about this blog</span>
    <p>
        <em>Paléo</em> was born from the wish to share a script as beautiful as it is
        little-known, without jargon or prerequisites. A remark, a question&nbsp;? The
        suggestion form at the bottom of the <a href="{{ path('paleo_en_glossaire') }}">glossary</a>
        is open.
    </p>
</div>
{% endblock %}
